[al:新概念英语（三）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:Speed and Comfort]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:00.31]Lesson 44 | 第44课
[00:02.17]Speed and comfort | 速度与舒适
[00:08.93]Which type of transport does the writer prefer, do you think? | 你认为作者更喜欢哪种交通方式？
[00:15.05]People travelling long distances frequently have to decide whether they would prefer to go by land, sea, or air. | 出远门的人常常需要决定是走陆路、海路还是坐飞机。
[00:23.94]Hardly anyone can positively enjoy sitting in a train for more than a few hours. | 几乎没有人能真正喜欢在火车上坐上好几个小时。
[00:30.98]Train compartments soon get cramped and stuffy. | 车厢很快会变得又拥挤又闷热。
[00:34.86]It is almost impossible to take your mind off the journey. | 想摆脱旅途的煎熬几乎是不可能的。
[00:39.10]Reading is only a partial solution, for the monotonous rhythm of the wheels clicking on the rails soon lull you to sleep. | 看书只能解决部分问题，因为车轮碾压铁轨的单调节奏很快就会催你入睡。
[00:49.10]During the day, sleep comes in snatches. | 白天，睡眠时断时续。
[00:52.90]At night, when you really wish to go to sleep, you rarely manage to do so. | 到了夜里你真想睡时，却很难睡着。
[00:58.60]If you are lucky enough to get a sleeper, | 即使你运气好，弄到了一个卧铺，
[01:01.43]you spend half the night staring at the small blue light in the ceiling, or fumbling to find your ticket for inspection. | 你也会半夜里盯着天花板上的小蓝灯，或者摸索着找车票以便查票。
[01:10.91]Inevitably you arrive at your destination almost exhausted. | 到达目的地时，你几乎已筋疲力尽。
[01:17.13]Long car journeys are even less pleasant, for it is quite impossible even to read. | 长途汽车旅行更加难受，因为连看书都几乎不可能。
[01:23.68]On motorways you can, at least, travel fairly safely at high speeds, | 在高速公路上，你至少能以较高的速度安全行驶，
[01:29.31]but more often than not, the greater part of the journey is spent on roads with few service stations and too much traffic. | 但更多的时候，旅程的大半时间是花在缺乏服务设施、交通拥挤的公路上。
[01:38.94]By comparison, ferry trips or cruises offer a great variety of civilized comforts. | 相比之下，渡船旅行或海上巡游则提供各种文明的舒适享受。
[01:46.94]You can stretch your legs on the spacious decks, play games, | 你可以在宽敞的甲板上伸展腿脚、玩游戏，
[01:51.00]meet interesting people and enjoy good food--always assuming, of course, that the sea is calm. | 结识有趣的人、享用美食——当然，这一切的前提是海上风平浪静。
[02:00.53]If it is not, and you are likely to get seasick, no form of transport could be worse. | 如果海上风浪大，你又容易晕船，那就没有比这更糟糕的交通方式了。
[02:08.15]Even if you travel in ideal weather, sea journeys take a long time. | 即使天气理想，海上旅行也需要很长时间。
[02:13.69]Relatively few people are prepared to sacrifice holiday time for the pleasure of travelling by sea. | 相对而言，没有多少人愿意牺牲假期的时间来换取海上旅行的乐趣。
[02:21.98]Aeroplanes have the reputation of being dangerous and even hardened travellers are intimidated by them. | 飞机有危险的名声，连老练的旅行者也畏而远之。
[02:29.86]They also have the disadvantage of being an expensive form of transport. | 飞机还有昂贵这一缺点。
[02:35.68]But nothing can match them for speed and comfort. | 但就速度与舒适而言，没有什么能与飞机相比。
[02:40.07]Travelling at a height of 30, 000 feet, far above the clouds, and at over 500 miles an hour is an exhilarating experience. | 在3万英尺的高空、云端之上，以每小时500多英里的速度飞行是一次令人振奋的经历。
[02:51.17]You do not have to devise ways of taking your mind off the journey, for an aeroplane gets you to your destination rapidly. | 你不必设法打发旅途的时间，因为飞机会迅速把你送到目的地。
[02:59.72]For a few hours, you settle back in a deep armchair to enjoy the flight. | 几个小时里，你靠坐在深深的扶手椅里享受旅程。
[03:06.26]The real escapist can watch a film and sip champagne on some services. | 真正会享受的人在某些航班上还可以看电影、呷香槟。
[03:12.79]But even when such refinements are not available, there is plenty to keep you occupied. | 但即使没有这些精美的享受，也有足够的事让你忙碌。
[03:18.57]An aeroplane offers you an unusual and breathtaking view of the world. | 飞机为你提供罕见而令人惊叹的俯瞰世界的视角。
[03:24.61]You soar effortlessly over high mountains and deep valleys. | 你毫不费力地飞越高山深谷。
[03:29.84]You really see the shape of the land. | 你真正看到了大地的形态。
[03:32.94]If the landscape is hidden from view, | 如果看不到地面的景观，
[03:35.59]you can enjoy the extraordinary sight of unbroken cloud plains that stretch out for miles before you, while the sun shines brilliantly in a clear sky. | 你可以欣赏眼前绵延数英里的一望无际的云海，同时明净的天空中阳光灿烂。
[03:48.89]The journey is so smooth that there is nothing to prevent you from reading or sleeping. | 旅途平稳，没有什么会妨碍你看书或睡觉。
[03:55.62]However you decide to spend your time, one thing is certain: you will arrive at your destination fresh and uncrumpled. | 无论你决定如何消磨时间，有一点是肯定的：你将精神饱满、毫无倦容地抵达目的地。
[04:05.57]You will not have to spend the next few days recovering from a long and arduous journey. | 你将不必花几天时间来从漫长而艰辛的旅途中恢复过来。
